REQUIRED SECRETS (CLIENT SETUP)
--------------------------------
The following secrets must be configured in GitHub repository settings:

| Secret Name        | Description              | Where to Find                     |
|--------------------|--------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| VERCEL_TOKEN       | Vercel API token         | https://vercel.com/account/tokens |
| VERCEL_ORG_ID      | Organization ID          | .vercel/project.json (orgId)      |
| VERCEL_PROJECT_ID  | Project ID               | .vercel/project.json (projectId)  |

Setup Instructions (for client):
1. Create Vercel account and link GitHub repository
2. Import project in Vercel dashboard
3. Run `vercel link` locally to generate .vercel/project.json
4. Extract orgId and projectId from .vercel/project.json
5. Create Vercel API token at https://vercel.com/account/tokens
6. Add all three secrets to GitHub repository settings

DEPLOYMENT WORKFLOW
-------------------

Automatic Deployments:

Preview (PR):
1. Developer creates pull request
2. CI workflow runs automatically (lint, type-check, test, build)
3. Deploy Preview workflow triggers
4. Application deploys to Vercel preview environment
5. Bot comments on PR with preview URL and testing checklist
6. Preview updates automatically on new commits

Production (Main):
1. PR is merged to main branch
2. CI workflow runs to verify quality
3. Deploy Production workflow triggers
4. Application deploys to Vercel with --prod flag
5. Deployment summary posted to GitHub Actions
6. Production URL updated immediately

Manual Deployments:
- Install Vercel CLI: npm i -g vercel
- Deploy preview: vercel
- Deploy production: vercel --prod

